<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barisone II of Arborea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1186</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Barisone I of Arborea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barisone II of Arborea was judge, or ruler, of the Judicate of Arborea in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1146. With money borrowed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> he had himself crowned King of Sardinia by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> at Pavia in 1164, aiming to rule the whole island. Unable to repay his debts, he was held in Genoa for years, and his royal title never gained real power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barisone-ii-of-arborea.jpg" alt="Barisone II of Arborea" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: René Tassin. Versement et modifications ː G.Garitan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barsone_rex_7006.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
